# Milestone: M3
# Covers: tag.block() called inside a tagged scope; block propagates from
#         the scope tag to the outer join ('&'); no deadlock.
# matrix-row: tag-block
#
# Rewritten from legacy tests/2.x/block-propagation.chk, whose `a` was an
# implicitly created tag; here it is declared in its own `run`.  This
# core's block is a gate (REVIVAL §14 S-tag-state-full), so the arm that
# blocks `a` holds the whole scope, the joining chunk included: the `run`
# hands back nil and `done` stays 0.  Nothing is wedged -- an unblock
# lets the join finish and the statement after the scope run.
## timeout: 30
## host: run var a = Tag.new()
## host: run var done = 0
## host: run a: { 1 & a.block() }; done = 1
## host: run done
## host: step 1000
## host: run a.unblock()
## host: run done
## host: step 1000
## host: live-work
[00000000] <Tag>
[00000000] 0
[00000000] nil
[00000000] 0
[00000000] step: QUIESCENT
[00000000] nil
[00000000] 1
[00000000] step: QUIESCENT
[00000000] live-work: false
